"""Script part 3: the interpreter's game commands and functions (script_vm.cpp past the script-level commands and its
helpers, script_functions.cpp's game functions), against the original's.

Run: script/build_cmd.bat, HD2_CMD_QUICK=1 (30,000 cases, about 20 s); MUT_EXTRA_SRCS original_exe.cpp and
cmd_calls.s, MUT_EXTRA_INC collision, MUT_LDFLAGS -Wl,--image-base=0x20000000; MUT_PASS "cmd_diff: .*, N checks, 0
failures". Prefixes: V script_vm.cpp, F script_functions.cpp, then the line.

Result (2026-11-23): 1,207 mutants, 153 not building; 1,017 of the 1,054 building killed, 37 survived. The first
quick run killed 900 of 1,058, a full-strength run of the rest 68 more; the other kills came after the test was made
stronger: it logs the structures passed by address (S_Explosion::Execute's, C_SoundModule::Play's request,
C_Debris::Setup's parameters), puts half the frames near the origin and some under a dummy near its box's faces (human
bodies and players in the boxes and ranges), sets the mission's time (Advance moves the script only once the mission
has started), seeds the cameras' FOV and range, the interface's hints and the script's HUD flags, logs an animation
set's play mode, draws numbers past the weather's clamps and play modes past the game types, adds a two-letter string,
and gives SetActorState 666 and the box commands a dummy often. (The unused IsActivePlayer was removed.) Survivors:
- Ties of floats (a value equal to the bound gives the same answer either way, or never occurs with these positions):
  the transformed box's min / max (V 45, 46, 47, 48, 49, 50 cmp; F 322, 323 cmp), the strict insides (V 56, F 330
  cmp), the nearest player's distance (V 517 cmp), the ranges (F 102, 237 cmp), the weather's clamps (V 1319, 1321,
  1346, 1347 cmp; V 1346 num: a length in whole mm is never between 0.0001 and 0.00015).
- Equivalent: Clamp255's 0 maps to 0 either way (V 32 cmp / num); a ninth box corner is corner 0 again (V 37, F 314
  cmp); a holster with no child answers GetChild(0) null (V 1231 cmp); PrintfNumber's buffer one byte longer (V 1060);
  the switch's default (no compiled script calls an unknown function: F 340); the actors list holds no null past the
  player slots (F 69 and).
- Unreachable: the commands' bad variable indices (the compiler writes only valid ones: V 534, 550 num, 564 and, 565
  bool, 790 and / num, 791 bool, 868 and, 869 bool).
- Rare: corner 0 left out of the transformed box, the first corner's min / max then uninitialized (V 41 num: a body in
  the strip that corner alone adds); a one-letter track on a train (V 802 num: "x" and "a" in a train's case).
"""
